  "tagline": "Ancient ram-leaping circle dance of shared identity",
  "profile": "Kochari (Քոչարի) is a traditional Armenian group folk dance from the Armenian highlands, performed in lines or semicircles with dancers holding hands or shoulders, featuring energetic knee bends and leaps that imitate horned animals; in Armenian the name means roughly \"knee-come\" (Wikipedia; UNESCO). It is danced by men and women of all ages to zurna and dhol, with a tempo ranging from moderate to fast and a lead dancer signalling figure changes.",
  "insight": "Kochari was inscribed on UNESCO's Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity on December 6, 2017 (decision 12.COM 11.b.2, Jeju, South Korea); UNESCO notes it \"provides a sense of shared identity and solidarity\" and is \"one of the rare traditional dances whose chain of transmission has never been interrupted.\"",
